---
description: Tacoma Telemetry project conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read README.md first. It defines the architecture and folder layout. Don't change the layout without asking.
- Backend is C++17, built with CMake. No raw new/delete: use RAII and smart pointers.
- Any data shared between threads needs a mutex or atomic, plus a one-line comment saying why.
- Vehicle data is a TelemetryFrame. Data sources implement ITelemetrySource. Never let simulator-specific code leak outside src/sim.
- Store values in OBD-native units (km/h, °C, rpm, percent). Convert to mph/°F only in the React UI.
- Every new class gets GoogleTest tests in backend/tests.
- Frontend is React + TypeScript (Vite). Keep telemetry message types in frontend/src/types.
- Keep changes small. Explain what you changed and why. Don't add dependencies without asking.
